-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 19 (part roc4), DIVISION 4 -- APPEALS FROM DISCIPLINARY TRIBUNAL UNDER MEDICAL REGISTRATION ACT (rule 41), LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT, and the time seams: as in roc4-order-19-div-1.l4 (imported for the time helpers).
-- Section 59G of the Medical Registration Act and section 2 (the meaning of "Disciplinary Tribunal") are borrowed facts, asked as inputs named for the section.
-- Paragraph (10) borrows rules from Divisions 1 and 3 of this Order, and paragraph (11) reads their "appellate Court" and "lower Court" as the General Division and the Disciplinary Tribunal.
-- This module does not restate those rules: it answers whether each applies (paragraphs (10) and (12)) and what the substituted courts are (paragraph (11)).
-- The caller reads the borrowed rule's own functions with the substituted courts (Seams, S-L1, in NOTES.md).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 19 -- Division 4 -- Appeals from Disciplinary Tribunal under Medical Registration Act`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 41 -- appeals under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 19 r 41(2) the period for the appellant's documents` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 8
    `period unit` IS Weeks
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

`o 19 r 41(3) the period for the respondent's documents` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 28
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:2822 | 41. —(1) A person who intends to appeal to the General Division under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act against a decision or order of a Disciplinary Tribunal must bring the appeal by filing and serving an originating application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal. [S 37/2024 wef 01/02/2024]
-- src:2823 | (2) The appellant must file and serve — ( a )
-- src:2824 | the record of proceedings;
-- src:2825 | ( b )
-- src:2826 | the appellant’s written submissions; and
-- src:2827 | ( c )
-- src:2828 | the appellant’s bundle of authorities,
-- src:2829 | within 8 weeks after the date on which the Registry informs the parties that the originating application has been fixed for hearing.
-- src:2830 | (3) The respondent must file and serve — ( a )
-- src:2831 | the respondent’s written submissions; and
-- src:2832 | ( b )
-- src:2833 | the respondent’s bundle of authorities,
-- src:2834 | within 28 days after the appellant serves the documents mentioned in paragraph (2) on the respondent.
-- src:2835 | (4) No affidavit is to be filed in an appeal brought under paragraph (1) without the permission of the General Division.
-- src:2836 | (5) The appellant’s written submissions and respondent’s written submissions are subject to a page limit of 55 pages, unless the General Division otherwise orders.
-- src:2837 | (6) The General Division may allow the page limit mentioned in paragraph (5) to be exceeded — ( a )
-- src:2838 | in special circumstances; and
-- src:2839 | ( b )
-- src:2840 | unless the General Division otherwise orders under paragraph (7), upon the payment of the fees and additional fees prescribed for the filing of pages in excess of the page limit.
-- src:2841 | (7) The General Division may upon application waive, refund, defer or apportion the payment of the fees mentioned in paragraph (6)( b ).
-- src:2842 | (8) There must not be more than one set of submissions for each party or set of parties represented by the same firm of solicitors unless the General Division otherwise orders.
-- src:2843 | (9) The concluding paragraphs of the written submissions must include — ( a )
-- src:2844 | submissions on the appropriate costs orders to be made in the appeal; and
-- src:2845 | ( b )
-- src:2846 | submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements that should be awarded in respect of all parties to the appeal.
-- src:2847 | (10) Subject to this Rule and any other written law, the following Rules in this Order apply to proceedings before the General Division under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act (including interlocutory applications): ( a )
