@ref O 19 r 41 (src:2822-2870)
GIVEN `the appeal is under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act against a decision or order of a Disciplinary Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is brought by an originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originating application is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 41(1) the appeal is brought by filing and serving an originating application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the appeal is under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act against a decision or order of a Disciplinary Tribunal`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) speaks only of "A person who intends to appeal to the General Division under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act against a decision or order of a Disciplinary Tribunal"
        IF `the appeal is brought by an originating application` AND `the originating application is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must bring the appeal by filing and serving an originating application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal"

