-- Paragraphs (10) and (12): which provisions of this Order apply to a section 59G appeal.
-- (10) lists the provisions that apply.  (12) says, to avoid doubt, that Division 1 (except Rule 1(f) and the provisions mentioned in (10)(a) to (e)) and Order 20 do not.
DECLARE `o 19 r 41(10) provision` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 41(10)(a) Rule 7 (Powers of appellate Court)`
    `o 19 r 41(10)(b) Rule 8 (Absence of parties)`
    `o 19 r 41(10)(c) Rule 10 (Withdrawal of appeal or application)`
    `o 19 r 41(10)(d) Rule 11 (Consent judgment or order)`
    `o 19 r 41(10)(e) Rule 12 (Judgment)`
    `o 19 r 41(10)(f) Rule 34 (Further arguments)`
    `o 19 r 41(10)(g) Rule 35(1) (Applications to appellate Court)`
    `o 19 r 41(10)(g) Rule 35(3) (Applications to appellate Court)`
    `o 19 r 41(10)(g) Rule 35(4) (Applications to appellate Court)`
    `o 19 r 41(10)(g) Rule 35(16) (Applications to appellate Court)`
    `o 19 r 41(10)(h) Rule 37 (Written submissions for applications to appellate Court)`
    `o 19 r 41(12)(a) Rule 1(f), which paragraph (12)(a) excepts`
    `o 19 r 41(12)(a) any other provision of Division 1 of this Order`
    `o 19 r 41(12)(b) Order 20`
    `o 19 r 41 any other provision of this Order or of these Rules`

@ref O 19 r 41(10) (src:2847-2862)
GIVEN provision IS A `o 19 r 41(10) provision`
      `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 41(10) the provision applies to proceedings under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(a) Rule 7 (Powers of appellate Court)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(b) Rule 8 (Absence of parties)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(c) Rule 10 (Withdrawal of appeal or application)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(d) Rule 11 (Consent judgment or order)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(e) Rule 12 (Judgment)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(f) Rule 34 (Further arguments)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(g) Rule 35(1) (Applications to appellate Court)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(g) Rule 35(3) (Applications to appellate Court)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(g) Rule 35(4) (Applications to appellate Court)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(g) Rule 35(16) (Applications to appellate Court)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(10)(h) Rule 37 (Written submissions for applications to appellate Court)` THEN `o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(12)(a) Rule 1(f), which paragraph (12)(a) excepts` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (10) does not list Rule 1(f), and paragraph (12)(a) only declines to exclude it
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(12)(a) any other provision of Division 1 of this Order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (10) does not list it; its exclusion is paragraph (12), which has its own function
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(12)(b) Order 20` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (10) does not list it; its exclusion is paragraph (12), which has its own function
    WHEN `o 19 r 41 any other provision of this Order or of these Rules` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (10) lists provisions and does not say "only"

-- A listed provision: it applies unless this Rule or another written law says otherwise.
GIVEN `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 41(10) listed provision applies` MEANS
    IF `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to this Rule and any other written law" -- the other provision is not named
    ELSE JUST TRUE

