-- src:2873 | “Disciplinary Tribunal” has the meaning given by section 2 of the Medical Registration Act;
@ref O 19 r 41(13) "Disciplinary Tribunal" (src:2873)
GIVEN `the body has the meaning of Disciplinary Tribunal given by section 2 of the Medical Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 41(13) a body is a Disciplinary Tribunal` MEANS
    IF `the body has the meaning of Disciplinary Tribunal given by section 2 of the Medical Registration Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Disciplinary Tribunal” has the meaning given by section 2 of the Medical Registration Act" -- the definition is handed to that section and no head of it holds

-- src:2874 | “record of proceedings” means any written grounds of decision, the record of evidence or notes of arguments taken, the affidavits or statutory declarations filed, as well as the submissions and any other documents tendered in respect of the proceedings before the Disciplinary Tribunal;
@ref O 19 r 41(13) "record of proceedings" (src:2874)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 41(13) document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 41(13) a document is part of the record of proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(13) written grounds of decision` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(13) the record of evidence or notes of arguments taken` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(13) an affidavit or statutory declaration filed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(13) a submission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 41(13) another document tendered in respect of the proceedings before the Disciplinary Tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“record of proceedings” means any written grounds of decision, the record of evidence or notes of arguments taken, the affidavits or statutory declarations filed, as well as the submissions and any other documents tendered in respect of the proceedings before the Disciplinary Tribunal"

-- src:2875 | “respondent” means the respondent in the originating application filed under paragraph (1). [S 37/2024 wef 01/02/2024]
@ref O 19 r 41(13) "respondent" (src:2875)
GIVEN `the person is the respondent in the originating application filed under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 41(13) a person is the respondent` MEANS
    IF `the person is the respondent in the originating application filed under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“respondent” means the respondent in the originating application filed under paragraph (1)"

